lines+=['','Intervals resample whole four-seat seed blocks. The results also include wider approximate six-comparison intervals for threat contrasts and fifteen-comparison intervals for direct card rankings. Multiple outcomes, sequential stopping and model/pilot bias make these exploratory estimates, not definitive population claims.','','## Engine preservation','','| Removed card | Ignition effect pp | Basic effect pp | Strong effect pp | Baseline / replacement threat median |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---|']
for a in arms:lines.append(f"| {a['removed']} | {a['contrasts']['ignition']['retention_effect_pp']:+.1f} | {a['contrasts']['basic']['retention_effect_pp']:+.1f} | {a['contrasts']['strong']['retention_effect_pp']:+.1f} | {f(a['baseline_timing']['threat_turn']['median'])} / {f(a['replacement_timing']['threat_turn']['median'])} |")
lines+=['','All timings are conditional on observing the event; no artificial late turn is assigned to failure. Full results include mean/median GGS cast, first/second Dragon and threat timing; one/two-turn Dragon conversion; conditional Basic/Strong/Threat rates; Dragons produced; peak board; Dragon damage; ammunition/access/resources; disruptions/recovery; stalls; and secondary wins. Conditioning only on ignition can select different games and is not the primary endpoint.','','## Exposure, casting and contribution','','| Amplifier | Baseline hand games | Baseline cast games | Material threat contributions | Whisper hand games | Whisper cast games |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for a in arms:lines.append(f"| {a['removed']} | {a['baseline_usage']['hand_games']} | {a['baseline_usage']['cast_games']} | {a['baseline_material_thresholds']['threat']} | {a['replacement_usage']['hand_games']} | {a['replacement_usage']['cast_games']} |")
lines+=['','Hand exposure includes observed tutored or stolen same-name cards; it is not restricted to ordinary draws or guaranteed original copies. Casting can be countered; presence is not automatically contribution. Exposure-only comparisons are descriptive. The original baseline’s 25 actual Throne type decisions all selected Human; GGS trigger amplification was not undermined by a wrong tribal choice.']

lines+=['','## Observed threat attribution','','Each cell is matched baseline / variant count. These within-game labels remain observational; slot-replacement effects do not prove that a contributing amplifier was indispensable. The other five amplifiers remain available.','','| Removed card | Natural GGS threats | Amplified GGS threats | Amplifier-dependent threats |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for a in arms:
 values=[str(a['baseline_dependency_counts']['threat'].get(k,0))+' / '+str(a['replacement_dependency_counts']['threat'].get(k,0)) for k in ['NATURAL GGS','AMPLIFIED GGS','AMPLIFIER-DEPENDENT']]
 lines.append('| '+a['removed']+' | '+' | '.join(values)+' |')
lines+=['','Basic and Strong attribution counts are preserved in the full results. A natural state may coexist with an amplifier that did not materially contribute; classification follows the observed path.']
