for a in arms:lines.append(f"- {a['removed']}: {a['valid']} valid; {a['stability']['slot_exposed_pairs']} slot-exposed pairs; stabilization {'passed' if a['stability']['passed'] else 'not met at the 128-game cap'}. Exact rate/timing shifts are recorded.")
lines+=['','The stopping rule requires at least 64 valid games, 20 exposed pairs, primary effects changing no more than 10 percentage points and observed median timing effects changing no more than one Pure turn. Stabilization is not the same as a narrow interval or proven equality.','','## Evidence-backed slot decisions','']
for a in sorted(arms,key=lambda a:a['contrasts']['threat']['retention_effect_pp'],reverse=True):
 c=a['contrasts']['threat'];wide=c['six_comparison_interval'];narrow=c['paired_seed_bootstrap_95']
 if wide[0]>0:decision='Evidence favors retaining this card over Whisper for pressure in this pod.'
 elif wide[1]<0:decision='Evidence favors the separate Whisper variant for pressure; combined cuts remain untested.'
 elif narrow[0]>0:decision='Promising retention signal, but not established under the wider six-comparison interval.'
 elif narrow[1]<0:decision='Promising replacement signal, but not established under the wider six-comparison interval.'
 else:decision='Individual slot value remains inconclusive; no justified indispensable/safe-cut claim.'
 lines+=[f"**{a['removed']}:** {decision} Threat retention effect {c['retention_effect_pp']:+.1f}pp; wider interval {ci(wide)}.",'']
lines +=[f"Direct ranking contrasts use the same **{R['common_comparison_games_per_arm']} common games per arm**, even when some arms extended farther. Positive A-over-B values mean removing A cost more pressure than removing B. The dataset preserves all pairwise intervals; an observed ordering alone is not a demonstrated ranking.",'','These tests measure whole-card opportunity cost versus a common ordinary draw spell with the other five amplifiers present. Tempest haste, Throne’s body/ward/trigger multiplication and extra-combat fresh-connection opportunities all count as real slot value. They do not isolate only damage text, test all-six-removed, identify each optimal replacement or justify adding six single-card effects together. Other cards or stolen amplifiers can compensate.','','## Definitions and interpretation','','The previous progression definitions were preserved. Basic requires another GGS Dragon within two following Pure turns and net meaningful board/resource growth. Strong includes 3 simultaneous GGS Dragons, 15 ready evasive power, multiple resolved creations in a turn, observed extra-combat compounding, or sustained engine draw/Treasure production. Threat is the operational proxy of 20 unblocked attacking power, 15 actual Pure combat damage in a turn, or 20 actual total Pure damage in a turn after ignition. Damage can be distributed among opponents; this proxy is not a guarantee of imminent table elimination or a model of human politics.','','Common seeds do not guarantee identical hands or trajectories once choices consume random numbers differently. Exact baseline gate replay agreement establishes restoration, not identical counterfactual variant games. Same pilot and pod make internal comparisons useful; confidence intervals do not capture human-play/model bias. No claim that every tactical choice was optimal.','','## Six representative paired logs','']
examples=[]
for a in arms:
 ms=[m for m in R['games'] if m['variant']==a['name'] and m['status']=='completed' and not m.get('excluded')]
 def score(m):
  b=B[m['seed'],m['rotation']];e=R['baseline_exposure'][f"{m['seed']}-r{m['rotation']}"]['cards'][a['removed']]
  return (e['hand_seen'] and m['inspection']['cards'][R['protocol']['replacement']]['hand_seen'],bool(b['threat_turn'])!=bool(m['threat_turn']),e['casts']>0,abs(b['cumulative_dragons']-m['cumulative_dragons']))
 m=max(ms,key=score);b=B[m['seed'],m['rotation']];examples.append((a,m,b));lines.append(f"- **{a['removed']}**, seed {m['seed']}, rotation {m['rotation']}: baseline D1/D2/threat={b['first_dragon_turn']}/{b['second_dragon_turn']}/{b['threat_turn']}; replacement={m['first_dragon_turn']}/{m['second_dragon_turn']}/{m['threat_turn']}. GGS Dragons produced {b['cumulative_dragons']} versus {m['cumulative_dragons']}. These selected illustrations do not replace aggregate evidence.")
zp=OUT/'Pure_GGS_Amplifier_Representative_Logs.zip'
